// Hanuman's Leap — sundara kanda
// Source: Valmiki, Sundara Kanda, sargas 1 (verify)
// Migrated from the old script format. Not yet staged for the Ramlila stage.

>> scene shore style=bharni-earth
>> music flight
>> cast hanuman at 0.4 scale=1.5
Mount Mahendra. He presses down with hands and feet until water runs out of the rock.
>> play holdRelease \{"who":"hanuman","time":1.5,"pose":\["crouch","crouch","crouch"\],"endPose":"jump","shake":9,"cue":"thunder","hint":"leap.2"\}
The mountain shakes. Trees torn up by the wind of him follow for a while, like friends seeing a traveller off.
>> scene ocean clear
>> play leap \{\}
>> scene lanka clear
>> enter hanuman from left to 0.3 in 1.2 scale=1
He comes down on a hill outside the city, not even breathing hard, and looks at the walls of gold.
>> scene ocean
>> set hanuman visible=false
>> wash
-> END
